<article class="env-lemma" id="08HT">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/08HT">Lemma <span data-tag="08HT">10.154.7</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a ring. Given a commutative diagram of ring maps </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ S \ar[r] &  K \\  R \ar[u] \ar[r] &  S' \ar[u] }  \]
</div>
  <p> where $S$, $S'$ are henselian local, $S$, $S'$ are filtered colimits of étale $R$-algebras, $K$ is a field and the arrows $S \to K$ and $S' \to K$ identify $K$ with the residue field of both $S$ and $S'$. Then there exists a unique $R$-algebra isomorphism $S \to S'$ compatible with the maps to $K$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Follows immediately from Lemma <a href="/tag/08HR" data-tag="08HR">10.154.6</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>